[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "adr-2608319600-itonami-is-a-hermes-profile-and-the-claude-oauth-patch-is-upstream"
  :adr/title "itonami is a hermes profile, and the Claude OAuth patch it would have carried is already upstream"
  :adr/status "accepted"
  :adr/date "2026-08-31"
  :adr/context
  "Asked to design an `itonami-claude-auth` plugin for the itonami CLI, mirroring
   `kristianvast/hermes-claude-auth` (Claude Code OAuth bypass for hermes-agent).

   Two measurements answered it instead.

   MEASUREMENT 1 — there is no itonami CLI.

     $ cat ~/.local/bin/itonami
     #!/bin/sh
     exec ~/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/hermes -p itonami \"$@\"

   itonami is one of 25 hermes profiles sharing one binary, one venv, one
   site-packages. hermes-claude-auth installs a `.pth` that monkey-patches
   `build_anthropic_kwargs` at interpreter startup, so a second copy under a
   second name would be a second `.pth` racing the first on the same
   interpreter. What is per-profile is `config.yaml`, `.env` and skills.
   `auth.json` and `credential_pool` live at $HERMES_HOME root and are shared.

   MEASUREMENT 2 — the patch is upstream in hermes-agent 0.20.6.

   With `~/.hermes/patches/` absent and no `.pth` installed, a one-shot call
   reached Anthropic and answered:

     $ itonami chat --provider anthropic -m claude-sonnet-4-6 -q 'Reply with exactly: OK' -Q
     OK

   agent.log for that turn:
     Lazy-installing anthropic==0.87.0 for feature 'provider.anthropic'
     provider=anthropic ... at https://api.anthropic.com
     API call #1: model=claude-sonnet-4-6 provider=anthropic in=15814 out=4 latency=4.1s

   The lazy install shows this was the first real Anthropic call on this
   machine, so no earlier state could have served it."

  :adr/decision
  "1. Do not create the repo. There is nothing for it to hold.

   2. Do not name anything `itonami-claude-auth`. Two independent reasons, and
      each would stand alone:
      (a) org elision (ADR-2608040170) — `cloud-itonami/itonami-claude-auth`
          says itonami twice.
      (b) the plane is wrong about the world — `plugin-` names the agent HOST
          it adapts (`manifest/repository-rules.edn`, ADR-2608318100, landed
          the same day). The host is hermes. itonami is a profile of that host,
          not a host. Had a repo been warranted, the name was
          `kotoba-lang/plugin-hermes-claude-auth`, or a surface on the existing
          `kotoba-lang/plugin-hermes`.

   3. Do not flip the itonami profile default to anthropic. Its default is
      `openrouter-free / z-ai/glm-5.3-flash`, which is a deliberate free-model
      floor (`scripts/hermes-hyakka-bots/free-model-policy.edn`) driving cron
      jobs. Claude on that profile is available per invocation via
      `--provider anthropic`; making it the default is a cost decision with an
      owner, and this is not it."

  :adr/evidence
  "Chain establishing that the successful call used the Claude Code OAuth
   token and nothing else:

   - `read_claude_code_credentials()` in the hermes venv returns
     source=macos_keychain, token kind sk-ant-oat (OAuth, not sk-ant-api),
     refresh token present, valid_now=true. Read by known identifier
     (Claude Code-credentials), not by enumeration.
   - No ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the session env, in `~/.hermes/.env`, in
     `~/.hermes/profiles/itonami/.env`, or in either config.yaml. The one
     secret the command helper injects is OPENROUTER_API_KEY from Keychain
     `gftd.openrouter`.
   - `hermes auth status anthropic` reports `logged out`;
     auth.json credential_pool holds only openrouter and copilot;
     active_provider is nil.
   - So the only anthropic credential present on the machine was the Claude
     Code OAuth token.

   Why hermes no longer needs the patch — `agent/anthropic_adapter.py`:
     - `build_anthropic_kwargs(..., is_oauth: bool = False)` docstring:
       'When is_oauth is True, applies Claude Code compatibility transforms:
       system prompt prefix, tool name prefixing, and prompt sanitization.'
     - `oauth-2025-04-20` is in the beta header list at line 480.
   These are the transforms hermes-claude-auth existed to inject. hermes now
   ships them first-party, so the third-party patch is obsolete here."

  :adr/consequences
  "Nothing is built and nothing is configured. The capability already exists
   and is reachable today with `itonami --provider anthropic -m <model>`.

   The load-bearing output of this ADR is negative: the next agent asked for
   `itonami-claude-auth` should read this instead of cloning a patch that
   would collide with hermes 0.20.6's own OAuth path.

   Two things would reopen it, and both are measurable rather than assumed:
   - a hermes update that removes the `is_oauth` transforms or the
     `oauth-2025-04-20` beta (re-run the one-shot smoke test; a 4xx from
     api.anthropic.com is the signal, not a fallback answering);
   - a decision to make Claude the itonami default, which is a change to the
     free-model policy and belongs to whoever owns that floor.

   Untested: whether the auto-discovery gate `is_provider_explicitly_configured`
   admits the Claude Code credentials without an explicit `--provider` flag.
   The smoke test passed the flag, so that path is UNVERIFIED rather than known
   to work."

